/-!
# Motivic cycle comparisons and real Deligne regulators: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. It records the roadmap's headline
theorems against the pinned APIs. None of the following headlines is statable at these pins:

* Layers 1.3–1.4: the integral cubical–simplicial comparison with supports, coefficients and
  operations lacks the face-admissible higher-cycle complexes and shared higher Chow groups.
* Layer 2.0a: Adams-compatible ordered relativity and multiplicative pairings for supported
  multi-relative cube K-theory lack scheme perfect K-spectra and their supported face
  diagrams, together with integral Adams operations on the associated pointed K-spaces.
  Integral Adams compatibility is asserted on those spaces and nonnegative homotopy groups.
* Layer 2.0b: the operations induced by the supplied universal integral motivic Chern
  classes lack scheme higher K-groups, higher Chow groups and their stabilized
  classifying-sheaf models.
* Layers 2.1–2.4: the geometric rational supported cycle-to-K comparison for regular
  quasi-projective schemes over every field, including full support, lacks supported scheme
  K-groups and higher-cycle restriction fibers. Its inverse agrees with the universal-class
  higher Chern character on smooth quasi-projective schemes; that identification and the
  smooth product theorem also lack these K-theory and motivic cohomology carriers.
* Layer 3.2: the geometric bifiltered logarithmic comparison and its shifted mixed Hodge
  data require the geometric logarithmic form sheaves, residue filtration and geometric
  Betti/de Rham comparison. Native linear mixed Hodge structures alone do not state it.
* Layer 3.3: the small real Deligne model and its cone deformation retract lack the real
  Dolbeault-complex carrier with its type projections and Deligne-model construction.
  Constructing that model is part of the roadmap, beyond a few simple definitions.
* Layer 3.4: compactification-independent Deligne realization, pullback and descent lack
  smooth SNC compactification diagrams, the Zariski-sheafified logarithmic Dolbeault
  algebra and its filtered Deligne complexes.
* Layers 4.1–4.2: the Deligne product, its natural associativity homotopy and the unit
  conclusion for unital inputs require real Dolbeault algebras and Deligne complexes,
  neither of which is available at these pins.
* Layer 5.2: singular-support semipurity and its normalized current criterion lack
  geometric Deligne cohomology with supports and the form/cycle-current comparison.
* Layer 5.4: the supported cycle-resolution and affine-contraction comparisons lack the
  good-position support diagrams and their truncated logarithmic Deligne total complexes.
* Layers 6.1–6.3: the universal derived regulator with coherent restriction fibers,
  pullback and model independence lacks both its integral motivic source and geometric
  Deligne target, together with their enhanced restriction diagrams.
* Layers 7.1–7.2: the independent Beilinson character and its equality with regulator
  composed with higher Chern character lack actual scheme higher K-groups, universal
  geometric Deligne Chern classes, and the two realization maps to be compared.
* Layer 7.3: multiplicativity of the regulator on integral higher Chow groups lacks those
  groups, geometric Deligne cohomology, their products and the universal regulator.

Ordinary scheme cycles, cochain complexes, derived categories and Dold–Kan supply underlying
infrastructure. They do not supply these missing geometric carriers. No weaker scalar
identity, free comparison predicate or assumed regulator is substituted for a headline.
-/

